# NOTE ON THE STL FILES, because this looked like a missing rule.
#
# Nothing is excluded here, deliberately. The superseded exports whose names
# contain spaces ("coxa new.stl", "femur top blah.stl" and the rest) are kept
# and TRACKED as CAD provenance: they show where the link meshes came from,
# which the report needs. "leg assembled.stl" is not provenance at all, it is
# a live input to tools/split_assembly.py, so it must be committed.
#
# What matters is that the URDF references only the re-origined files
# (coxa.stl, femur.stl, tibia.stl, body.stl). A filename containing a space
# breaks package:// resolution, so the originals must never be referenced
# even though they are stored.
